    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0390" n="316" xml:id="pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/816</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-15T17:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 15, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.35 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7980. I had an informal talk on December 4 with Lord
                        Robert Cecil, on the subject treated in telegram 1653, December
                    1, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d306-f1"/> from the Copenhagen Legation, which
                    was transmitted to the Department through me.</p>
                <p>Mr. Balfour now informs me that should you
                    see fit to take any steps to prevent the recognition of the Bolshevik government
                    by neutral powers the British Government is ready to lend its support.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
